From e7ed70c63a66fc16166fcc75bde6539ecfc60039 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: japq7s <japiotr123@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 14:30:05 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 12/32] ipa: simple: Add contrast detection autofocus

Add an Af algorithm for the soft IPA, enabled by an Af entry in the
tuning file, using the focus measure of the software ISP statistics
normalised by the squared mean luminance.

A scan steps the lens from infinity towards macro in coarse steps until
the measure has clearly passed its peak, then scans around the best
position in fine steps and settles on the peak interpolated from its
neighbours. A scan with no clear peak ends in AfStateFailed with the
lens at infinity.

In AfModeContinuous, the default, the lens is left alone once focused:
a new scan only starts when the focus measure or the brightness have
moved away from their values at the end of the last scan for several
measurements, and the scene has then been stable for several more. This
keeps the lens from hunting while the camera moves or because of noise
in a dim scene. AfModeAuto scans on AfTriggerStart, AfModeManual moves
the lens to LensPosition, mapped linearly from 0 (infinity) to
macroDioptres onto the lens range.

Tuning parameters: infinity and macro (lens positions, default the lens
range), macroDioptres (default 10), coarseSteps (12), fineSteps (4).

Signed-off-by: japq7s <japiotr123@proton.me>
